Improved: IBTK::FACPreconditioner::initializeSolverState() on an initialized preconditioner now calls the new IBTK::FACPreconditionerStrategy::reinitializeOperatorState(). By default, this function deallocates and initializes the operator. IBTK::CCPoissonPointRelaxationFACOperator, IBTK::CCPoissonBoxRelaxationFACOperator, IBTK::CCPoissonLevelRelaxationFACOperator, IBTK::SCPoissonPointRelaxationFACOperator, and IBTK::VCSCViscousOpPointRelaxationFACOperator now reuse the data that depend only on the layout. Examples are the schedules, the coarse-fine fills, and the vector clones. The operators reuse these data when the hierarchy and the vectors are unchanged. They rebuild only the data that depend on the coefficients and the boundary conditions.
<br>
(Boyce Griffith, 2026/11/26)
